                                "example_id": "9a151983-3355-42d7-81ee-3842a8426cc6",
                                "sense_id": "85dc5236-3e24-31db-90b9-52c33ffe6442",
                                "text": "\"Don't you have a dodie for her?” \"Dodie?\" \"Ah...\" Blaine hesitated. \"Pacifier.\" \"Oh! It's one of those things I haven't gotten yet. She doesn't seem to look for one.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "df47cc72-048a-4225-b6b2-03b9704cdaf4",
                                "sense_id": "85dc5236-3e24-31db-90b9-52c33ffe6442",
                                "text": "\"Dodie trees\" are not often associated with holy wells; in fact, the young child finishing with nursing or teething can be asked to give the dodie (teether or pacifier) to the fairies by letting family members hang it on a tree."
                            }
